###  http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualConsistencyScore
:IndividualConsistencyScore rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                     :DistanceBasedFairnessMetric ;
                            :extends :ConsistencyScore ;
                            :hasBeenAppliedTo :LawAndJustice ;
                            :isProposedBy papers:2025_WALLER ;
                            :measures :FairnessThroughAwareness ;
                            :refersTo :Classification ;
                            :scientificArtifactDescription """It is an extension of the consistency score, which does not provide an overall (average) evaluation of the individual fairness performance of the predictor, but is able to asses how fair the model is for any individual in the dataset. Given a binary classifier $f$ for a dataset $E$ and an individual $x \\in E$, 
the individual consistency score $c_{\\sigma,k}(x)$ computes the proportion of 
$x$'s $k$ most similar individuals (according to $\\sigma$) that receive the same 
classification as $x$:
\\[
c_{\\sigma,k}(x)
= 1 - \\left| f(x) - \\frac{1}{k} 
\\sum_{y \\in {nbr}_{\\sigma}(x,k)} f(y) \\right| .
\\]""" .


