###  http://fairness_ontology.com/ControlOffensiveTokens
:ControlOffensiveTokens rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                 :DecisionTimeConstrainedDecisioning ;
                        :isProposedBy papers:2020_XU ;
                        :scientificArtifactDescription "use word- or ngram-blocking during decoding, prohibiting the use of tokens from an offensive word list. The authors identify control tokens using a classifier that measures offensiveness, bias, and other potential harms in text. The control tokens can be appended to the input during inference to control model generation." .



###  http://fairness_ontology.com/ConsistencyScore
:ConsistencyScore rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                           :DistanceBasedFairnessMetric ;
                  :hasBeenAppliedTo :Healthcare ;
                  :isEquivalentTo :FairnessThroughAwareness ;
                  :isProposedBy papers:2013_ZEMEL ;
                  :isUsedBy papers:2025_WALLER ;
                  :measures :FairnessThroughAwareness ;
                  :refersTo :Classification ;
                  :scientificArtifactDescription """It measures the overall level of disparity in the classification of individuals with respect to similar individuals, using the k nearest neighbours.  To do so, $yNN$ gives a value in the interval [0, 1], and the higher the value, the lower the level of disparity overall: $y_{\\mathrm{NN}} 
= 1 - \\frac{1}{N_k} \\sum_{n}
\\left| \\hat{y}_n - \\sum_{j \\in k\\text{-NN}(x_n)} \\hat{y}_j \\right| $, where $x_n$ is one of the $N$ examples in the training set.""" ;
                  skos:definition "The aggregation potentially masks high levels of disparity for particular individuals. Very similar to Fairness through awareness, but does not require domain knowledge to define 𝑑." .


